                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I hate to not recommend any Zachtronics game.  It runs fine, looks good, no bugs or issues.  So what's the problem?  For me, it was the gameplay.  Everything good that I like has some kind of caveat that I don't like.  This is one of those games where they did many things poorly instead of doing a fewer things well.\r\n\r\n✅Turn-based combat / ❌Turns are on an automatic timer\r\n✅Action point (AP) system / ❌Few options to get more AP faster depending on the map\r\n✅Deck-builder / ❌Puzzle-like nature of the levels means you're fiddling with your deck a lot\r\n✅Lots of cards to unlock / ❌I felt like it took too long to get \"useful\" cards - especially early-game\r\n\r\n\r\nI like the idea of the game.  I feel like if it were just a deck-builder or just turn-based strategy then I'd love it.  But as it is, it's like you start a battle to see the new unit or special spot on the map, quit the battle to completely rebuild or at least tweak your deck to deal with that, then start the battle again and hope you get the cards that will get you through this new thing.  The timer-turns + AP/turn system is also annoying as you're mostly looking at your cards with the \"NOT ENOUGH AP\" banner across them waiting for the game to let you play.\r\n\r\nI completed the campaign in 2017 and never wrote a review.  I revisited the game recently to see why.  In summary, I would describe this game as disappointing.  I kept waiting for that \"ah-ha, here is the fun part\" which never happened.",
